# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-normalised-form-reals-autocad -- a form alfe's normaliser rewrites still loses real digits on AutoCAD
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-alfe-normalised-form-reals
#+DATE: 2026-10-08

* Symptom

After alfe-cad-transport-rounds-reals (2.3.12), literals sent as source reach
the CAD exact, but a form the AutoCAD princ/load normaliser REWRITES (a
1-argument princ/print/prin1/load padded to 2 arguments) is re-printed on
the CAD side, and AutoCAD's rtos cannot render every double exactly
(real-transport probe, jobs 17033116729 GUI / 17033116730 accoreconsole):

#+begin_example
REALTX b normalised differs REAL 1.570796326794895 1.570796326794895E+00
REALTX i normalised differs REAL 1.797693134862313E+99 1.797693134862313E+99
REALTX j normalised differs REAL 1.234567890123456E+17 1.234567890123456E+17
#+end_example

8 of 11 cases are exact; BricsCAD is exact on all 11.

* Fix

Do not re-print: rewrite the normalised call in the SOURCE TEXT, as
alfe-open-rewrite-text does for OPEN (MR !467) -- pad `(princ X)` to
`(princ X nil)` textually, leaving every other character (and every real
literal) as written; fall back to the lossless printer only when the text
rewrite cannot be verified by reading it back.

* Fix (2026-10-22)

Branch fix-alfe-normalised-form-reals. Stays NEXT until the real-transport
probe has MEASURED it on AutoCAD (jobs =real-transport:probe:autocad:windows=
and =real-transport:probe:accoreconsole:windows= in =.gitlab/native.yml=;
the Windows runners are back 2026-10-23): expected =normalised exact= on all
11 cases, b, i and j included.

** What

The normalised form is no longer re-printed: its SOURCE TEXT is rewritten,
as =alfe-open-rewrite-text= does for OPEN. In
=autolisp-front-end/source/runtime/autolisp-bootstrap.lsp=:

- =alfe-normalize-princ-text= -- the textual twin of
  =autolisp-normalize-princ-call-impl=. It scans the text (strings, =;= and
  =;| |;= comments skipped), counts the elements of each list as the reader
  sees them (='X= is one), and at the closing parenthesis of an unquoted
  call pads it: 1-argument princ/print/prin1/load get " nil" inserted
  before the parenthesis; an empty (princ) has its head replaced by
  =autolisp-princ-newline=; an empty (print) / (prin1) gets ~ "" nil~.
  Lists quoted by ='= or headed by QUOTE / FUNCTION, and lists in HEAD
  position (the form walker never descends into a head), are left alone,
  as the walker does. Every other character -- every real literal -- is
  kept as written.
- =alfe-normalized-source-text (form normalized source)= -- the text for the
  normalised form: SOURCE itself when the normaliser returned FORM (EQ),
  else SOURCE through =alfe-normalize-princ-text=; in both cases used only
  if READ of it is EQUAL to the (normalised) form, else NIL.
- =alfe-text-splice-edits= -- the splice loop, now shared by both rewriters.
- =alfe-open-request-text= starts from =alfe-normalized-source-text=, so a
  form that calls OPEN AND was padded keeps its text too (it used to be
  printed).

In =source/file-protocol.lisp= the emitted =alfe-request-source-text= uses
=alfe-normalized-source-text= and falls back to =autolisp-form-source-text=
(the printer) only when that returns NIL: no source text (a form built in
memory), or a rewrite that does not read back as the normalised form (a
dotted list, a reader syntax the scan does not know).

The user manual's "How a form reaches a CAD" section says so.

** Tests (autolisp-front-end/tests/file-protocol-tests.lisp)

- =protocol-normalize-princ-text-pads-in-the-source=: 12 textual cases
  (1-arg princ/print/prin1/load padded, empty (princ) and (print), 2-arg
  calls untouched, nested calls, strings, comments, quote / function, head
  position) plus =alfe-normalized-source-text= returning the padded text for
  the matching source and NIL for a non-matching or missing one.
- =protocol-normalised-form-reals-reach-the-engine-exactly= (hosted
  clautolisp-sbcl on the AutoCAD fixed-arity path, =:assume-no-rest-p t=,
  the real printer stubbed to =(rtos x 1 15)= -- 16 significant digits, as
  AutoCAD's rtos -- and counting its calls):
  =(setq rtn-p (princ 1.5707963267948966))= and
  =(progn (setq rtn-j 123456789012345678.0 rtn-e 1.2345678901234567) (princ ""))=
  arrive exact, the printer called 0 times.
  RED against the old code: =RTN P ROUNDED J ROUNDED E ROUNDED PRINTED 3=.
  GREEN after: =RTN P EXACT J EXACT E EXACT PRINTED 0=.
- =protocol-real-literals-reach-the-engine-exactly=: the fixed-arity path
  now re-prints nothing either (=REPRINTED no= on both paths; it was =yes=).

=make -C autolisp-front-end test-sbcl= and =test-ccl=: Fail: 0.
